 "researcher_notes": "A federal filing from November 2025 (docket CP26-28-000) says Rockies Express Pipeline LLC asked to build about 7.2 miles of new 36-inch pipe, a new interconnect at its Cheyenne Hub in Weld County, Colorado, and a meter station in Laramie County, Wyoming. It would add 419,000 dekatherms per day of firm service for $57.3 million. The filing says the gas fuels a planned power plant in an industrial park. A Tallgrass press release from May 2026 says the Cheyenne Power Hub, about 1,150 megawatts, is fueled by gas from Rockies Express and will power a large data center in the Switchgrass Industrial Park. A press report from August 2025 describes the Crusoe and Tallgrass data center and power plant campus in Cheyenne. Not the same as the Cheyenne Hub Enhancement row (P2517, a compression expansion), the Cheyenne Connector row (P0359), or the Critical Energy Reliability Link row (P7863, 160 miles). No existing row has the Switchgrass name. Status is proposed because reports of the in-service date conflict (October 2026 in some, early 2028 in others) and none confirms construction. The filing does not state a month or a year of start, so those cells are blank. Owner spelled as in the ownership team's existing entity. Route not found; no official map checked."
